Description: enable V-Sync, fix the audio format and the -w option
 The SDL2 port opened the audio device with SDL_AUDIO_ALLOW_ANY_CHANGE:
 the callback always writes signed 16-bit stereo samples and the analysis
 reads BLKSIZE*2 samples, so a server providing float samples or another
 buffer size (PipeWire) gave noise or out-of-bounds reads. Let SDL convert
 instead.
 .
 Enable V-Sync after the creation of the OpenGL context, and sleep for 1 ms
 when the 100 Hz limiter skips a frame instead of spinning on the CPU.
 .
 Clear the fullscreen flag with a mask: subtracting it twice (-w option and
 program name ending with w) gave invalid window flags.
